# Build-time configuration for the web app.
#
# Copy to `.env.local` (which is gitignored, and survives the `git checkout` a
# deploy performs) and edit, then rebuild:
#
#     cp website/.env.example website/.env.local
#     cd website && npm run build
#
# The BACKEND is configured separately, in the systemd unit's EnvironmentFile —
# WORK_TIME_SIGNUP_MODE and friends live there, not here. See backend/DEPLOYMENT.md.


# ── What gets built ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The tracker, dashboard and reports. Nothing to configure: tracksuite.work's
# landing page and marketing are never part of your build, so `/` goes straight
# to the tracker (or the sign-in page).


# ── Where the source lives ───────────────────────────────────────────
# The footer links to the repository, its LICENSE and its issue tracker. If you
# run a fork, point this at your own repo — otherwise your users file bugs
# against code you no longer run.
#VITE_REPO_SLUG=yourname/your-fork


# ── Operator details for the legal pages ─────────────────────────────
# If VITE_LEGAL_NAME is empty on an app-only build, NO legal pages are published
# and no footer links appear — the right answer for an internal company instance
# already covered by the company's own privacy notice and imprint.
#
# If you publish an instance to the open internet from the EU, filling these in
# is not optional: Austria (§ 25 MedienG, § 5 ECG) and Germany (§ 5 DDG) both
# require a reachable imprint, and Art. 13 GDPR requires a privacy notice naming
# the controller. The pages render a visible warning while any mandatory field is
# missing.

# Which country's disclosure and consumer-protection rules the pages follow:
# `at` (default), `de`, or anything else for a generic English imprint. This
# picks the statutes cited, the liability clause, the data-protection authority
# and the governing law — set it before anything else.
#VITE_LEGAL_JURISDICTION=at

# Only needed when VITE_LEGAL_JURISDICTION is neither `at` nor `de`: the country
# whose law governs the Terms, spelled out.
#VITE_LEGAL_JURISDICTION_NAME=Switzerland

# Full legal name of the operator (natural person or company). Required.
#VITE_LEGAL_NAME=Jane Doe

# Street and house number. Required unless VITE_LEGAL_SMALL_WEBSITE=1 below.
# A PO box never suffices.
#VITE_LEGAL_STREET=Musterstraße 1

# Postal code and city. Required. At the reduced Austrian disclosure the city
# alone is what gets published, so write just the city there.
#VITE_LEGAL_CITY=1010 Wien

# Country. Defaults to Austria on the public build.
#VITE_LEGAL_COUNTRY=Austria

# What the site is for ("Unternehmensgegenstand"). Required by § 25 MedienG for
# the reduced Austrian disclosure; harmless elsewhere.
#VITE_LEGAL_BUSINESS_PURPOSE=Non-commercial operation of open-source work-time tracking software

# AUSTRIA ONLY — publish the reduced disclosure of § 25 Abs 5 MedienG: name,
# place of residence (city, no street) and business purpose.
#
# This is available to a "kleine Website": one that presents nothing beyond the
# operator's own personal or business life and has no influence on public
# opinion. A plain product site for a free tool generally qualifies; a site with
# a blog, news, comments or opinion pieces does NOT, and then you owe the full
# disclosure including a street address.
#
# Note this only removes the MEDIA-law address. § 5 ECG separately requires a
# geographic address of *commercial* providers ("Diensteanbieter"). A genuinely
# free, non-commercial project has a good argument that § 5 ECG does not apply to
# it at all — but it is an argument, not a certainty, and the fine is up to
# €3,000. If you monetise in any way (ads, donations tied to features, a paid
# tier, affiliate links), do not use this: rent a c/o business address instead.
#
# Ignored unless VITE_LEGAL_JURISDICTION=at.
#VITE_LEGAL_SMALL_WEBSITE=1

# A mailbox you actually monitor. Required.
#VITE_LEGAL_EMAIL=contact@example.com

# Optional. Only publish a number you're willing to have publicly listed.
#VITE_LEGAL_PHONE=+49 30 123456

# Optional: VAT ID per § 27a UStG. Omit entirely if you are not VAT-registered.
#VITE_LEGAL_VAT_ID=DE123456789

# Optional but recommended: who hosts the server, named in the privacy policy as
# a processor. Omitted, the policy falls back to the generic wording Art. 13
# also permits ("our hosting provider").
#VITE_LEGAL_HOSTING=Hetzner Online GmbH, Gunzenhausen, Germany

# Transactional email processor. Set to empty on an instance that sends no email
# (no RESEND_API_KEY) so the policy doesn't claim a transfer that never happens.
#VITE_LEGAL_EMAIL_PROVIDER=

# Shown as "last updated" on the legal pages. Keep in step with the backend's
# WORK_TIME_TOS_VERSION, which records the version each account accepted.
#VITE_LEGAL_EFFECTIVE_DATE=2026-07-27

# Branding.
#VITE_LEGAL_SITE_NAME=Acme Time
#VITE_LEGAL_SITE_DOMAIN=time.acme.com
